{"study_accession":"PRJNA1051962","secondary_study_accession":"SRP477736","title":"Analysis of MTX-3937-treated human peripheral NK cells","description":"Siglec-9 has been of particular interest for their potential as immune checkpoints. Here, we employed docking-based virtual screening combined with bio-layer interferometry assays to identify a potential Siglec-9 inhibitor, MTX-3937. Analysis showed that MTX-3937-treatment significantly enhanced the production of IFN-γ, TNF-α, perforin and CD107a in human NK cells. Consistently, MTX-3937 largely promoted NK cells tumor killing activities both in vitro and in vivo. In mechanism, MTX-3937 inhibited the phosphorylation level of SHP-1/2 in NK92 cells. Overall design: To globally characterize MTX-3937-mediated improvement of NK cell functions, we assessed the transcriptional profiles of MTX-3937- and DMSO-treated human peripheral NK cells from healthy donors.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":4,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN38809662","study_accession":"PRJNA1051962","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"MTX-3937_2","description":"MTX-3937_2","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7973464","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2024-01-13","attributes":[["source_name","Peripheral NK cells"],["tissue","Peripheral NK cells"],["genotype","WT"],["treatment","MTX-3938"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR27197221","experiment_accession":"SRX22877308","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"DNBSEQ-T7","read_count":23807719,"base_count":1190385950,"first_public":"2024-01-13","experiment_title":"DNBSEQ-T7 sequencing: GSM7973464: MTX-3937_2 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN38809663","study_accession":"PRJNA1051962","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"MTX-3937_1","description":"MTX-3937_1","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7973463","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1